  "tagline": "Small-footprint, clusterable time-series database with a query language built for grouping series.",
  "description": "SiriDB is an open-source time-series database written in C and maintained by the Dutch company Cesbit. Series are distributed over pools that can be added while the database is online, each pool optionally mirrored by a replica, and the design avoids a global index so a cluster can grow without downtime. Its own query language is good at selecting and grouping thousands of series with regular expressions and dynamic groups, and the project ships an HTTP server, a Grafana data source and Python, Go and Node.js connectors. Releases still arrive in 2026, but the community is small, so treat it as a niche choice.",
